                    briefing_text_r1:       `It is the day of the PE owner’s first quarterly review. Revenue is at a record €410M, but operating margin has slipped to <strong>6.5%</strong> and free cash flow is weak. You have the customer-and-product dataset and the current KPI inventory. Run a real customer-profitability analysis: <strong>load true cost-to-serve</strong> onto each account and rank by <em>operating</em> profit — not revenue, not gross margin. Build the whale curve, locate the loss-making tail (~€6.5M a year, masked by gross-margin reporting), name the few cost-to-serve drivers — <em>order frequency, expedited freight, returns</em> — and show how the revenue-based commission rewards exactly the wrong customers.`,
