                    coach_default:          `Decision logged.`,
                    coach_r1_costtoserve:   `<strong>That is the analysis that tells the truth.</strong> Loading order frequency, freight, returns, support and the financing of payment terms onto each account turns gross margin into <em>operating</em> profit per customer. The whale curve appears: a minority earn all the profit while a tail destroys it. Now you can see the €6.5M nobody could.`,
                    coach_r1_grossmargin:   `<strong>Gross margin is exactly what hid the problem.</strong> It is managed by product line and ignores cost-to-serve entirely — small frequent orders, expedited freight, returns, extended terms. Two customers with identical gross margin can sit at opposite ends of the whale curve. Load the true cost-to-serve.`,
                    coach_r1_revenue:       `<strong>“The big accounts are the good accounts” is the belief destroying your margin.</strong> Your single most operating-unprofitable account is also your biggest commission earner. Rank by revenue and you will protect exactly the customers bleeding you. Rank by operating profit after cost-to-serve.`,
